// test_qt_bridge_io_clipboard_registration.hv — guards the extraction of
// io.getClipboard out of the core-facing bridge TUs.
//
// What: resolves io.getClipboard and invokes it, asserting the reference is a
//       registered host function rather than nil.
// Why:  io.getClipboard was glue at the bottom of the core-facing
//       extensions/gui/clipboard_manager/ClipboardManager.cpp. It now lives in
//       src/host/module/bridges/qt/QtBridge.cpp (havel_gui target only) and is
//       installed through the explicit BridgeSelection slot that src/main.cpp
//       fills with installQtBridge. A registration lost in that move makes the
//       bare reference below resolve to nil, and the assert fails with
//       "io.getClipboard must be registered by the Qt bridge" — observed, exit 1.
// Expected: assert passes.
//
// Deliberately NOT asserted on the returned text:
//   - reading an X11 clipboard can transfer ownership, so a second read in the
//     same process can legitimately come back empty. Headless (nil) and desktop
//     (text) runs therefore disagree, and no value assertion is stable in both.
//   The registration, not the payload, is what this test guards.
//
// Non-vacuity evidence: renaming the registration key in QtBridge.cpp from
// "io.getClipboard" to garbage and rebuilding makes this test exit 1 with the
// assertion message above. That is how this test was validated.
//
// Note on the neighbouring clipboard.* names: clipboard.get / clipboard.set /
// clipboard.clear are ALSO registered by the opt-in clipboard module plugin
// (src/modules/clipboard/ClipboardModule.cpp), so those names resolve even when
// the Qt bridge is absent and cannot discriminate. io.getClipboard and
// gui.notify are registered by QtBridge and nothing else, which is why they are
// the names guarded here and in test_gui_notify_registration.hv.

getClipboardRef = io.getClipboard

assert(getClipboardRef != nil, "io.getClipboard must be registered by the Qt bridge")

// Invoke it. Without a clipboard manager the bridge returns nil; with one it
// reads the real clipboard. Either way the call must not throw, and the
// registration was already proven above.
observed = io.getClipboard()

print("qt bridge io.getClipboard registration: ok")
